-- title:
--   Determinant of σ - c on a cyclic extension
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $E$ be fields with $E$ an $F$-algebra that is finite-dimensional over $F$, and write $n = \dim_F E$. Let $\sigma \colon E \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[F]} E$ be an $F$-algebra automorphism of $E$ whose order in the automorphism group is exactly $n$, and let $c \in E$. Consider the $F$-linear endomorphism of $E$ obtained by subtracting from the underlying $F$-linear map of $\sigma$ the scalar multiple $c \cdot \mathrm{id}$, that is, the map $x \mapsto \sigma(x) - cx$ (scalar multiplication by $c$ acting on $F$-linear endomorphisms of $E$ through the $E$-module structure). Its determinant is an element of $F$, and the assertion is that its image under the structure map $F \to E$ equals
--   $$(-1)^{\,n-1}\Bigl(1 - \prod_{i=0}^{n-1} \sigma^i(c)\Bigr),$$
--   the product being taken over $i$ in the range $0,\dots,n-1$ and the exponent $n-1$ being truncated natural subtraction. The hypothesis on the order of $\sigma$ forces $E/F$ to be Galois and cyclic with group generated by $\sigma$, so the product is the norm $N_{E/F}(c)$ and the identity takes place in the image of $F$.
--
--   This is the classical computation of the determinant of $\sigma - c$ on a cyclic extension, giving $\det_F(\sigma - c) = (-1)^{n-1}(1 - N_{E/F}(c))$, the identity underlying the appearance of norm forms in twisted trace formula computations. It is used in the project's computations with automorphic forms and in a local index computation for completions at height-one primes of a Dedekind domain.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgEquiv_algebraMap_det_toLinearMap_sub_smul_id_eq_of_orderOf_eq_finrank.lean

